Overview

This program is a Flask-based web application that visualizes network topology from parsed interface files. It reads .txt files, extracts network connection details, and generates an interactive network topology visualization using PyVis.

1️⃣ HTML Frontend (index.html)

Explanation:

Defines a webpage for network visualization.

<button> triggers topology generation via Flask API.

<iframe> loads the generated network visualization.

JavaScript (loadTopology) updates the iframe with /generate_topology route.

2️⃣ Flask Backend (app.py)

Explanation:

Imports necessary modules:

flask: Handles web routes (Flask, render_template, send_file).

os: Manages file operations.

re: Handles regular expressions for parsing network files.

xml.etree.ElementTree: Allows XML processing (if needed for Draw.io).

networkx: Graph visualization and data structure.

pyvis: Creates interactive visualizations.

Explanation:

Creates a Flask web app instance.

Defines FOLDER_PATH where network topology .txt files are stored.

3️⃣ NetworkTopology Class

Initialization

Initializes the class with the folder path and an empty NetworkX graph.

Parsing Network Files

Reads lines from the network file.

Extracts the hostname from the file name using regex.

Stores the extracted hostname.

Initializes an empty interfaces list.

Uses regex to match network connections in each line.

Extracts interface name, admin/oper status, remote device, and remote interface.

Filters out unwanted interfaces like irb, lo0, and ps.

Determines if the link is down and stores it.

Building Topology

Iterates through .txt files and parses them.

Adds network connections to the NetworkX graph with red/green color coding.

Generating Interactive Visualization

Creates a PyVis interactive visualization.

Adds nodes with a blue color.

Adds edges with green/red based on status.

Saves the interactive visualization in /static/.

4️⃣ Flask Routes

Serves the index.html web page.

Generates the topology and serves the visualization file.

5️⃣ Running the App

Starts the Flask web server in debug mode.

🎯 Summary

✅ Parses network interface files
✅ Builds a NetworkX graph
✅ Generates an interactive PyVis visualization
✅ Serves it via Flask as a web app

